message:
Fix #163192: Memory leak on WM_exit after recent commit

Caused by 5fe06581927caf675ae2cc05361a96a15b1afe76
This looks to be a real leak, a bug in the library most likely
(see minimal reproduction below). It also looks like our lsan
suppression list would have stopped this from being reported
in the past, but no longer does after a recent TBB library update.
Add the new namespace `tbb::detail::r1`.

```
class Observer : public tbb::task_scheduler_observer {
public:
  Observer() { observe(true); }
  ~Observer() override { observe(false); }
};

int main() {
  Observer *observer = new Observer();
  tbb::parallel_for(tbb::blocked_range<int>(0, 1000000), [](const auto &) {});
  delete observer;
  return 0;
}
```

Pull Request: https://projects.blender.org/blender/blender/pulls/163114

Fix: MSVC warning

warning C4927: illegal conversion;
more than one user-defined conversion has been implicitly applied

Fix #156481: EEVEE: Some node combinations can corrupt the Raycast node across the entire scene

The problem was that `eevee_shader` may add different engine texture
slots to materials within the same pass.

````cpp
if (GPU_material_flag_get(gpumat, GPU_MATFLAG_RAYCAST) &&
      ELEM(pipeline_type, MAT_PIPE_DEFERRED, MAT_PIPE_FORWARD))
{
    info.additional_info("eevee_raycast");
}

if (ELEM(pipeline_type, MAT_PIPE_DEFERRED, MAT_PIPE_FORWARD) &&
      GPU_material_flag_get(gpumat, GPU_MATFLAG_SHADER_TO_RGBA))
{
    info.additional_info("eevee_hiz_prev_data");
    info.additional_info("eevee_previous_layer_radiance");
}
````

Since we bind pass resources at the pass start, if the `SlotAllocator`
uses those for any other material, other materials within the same pass
may have the wrong resources bound.

This PR ensures that materials with different engine-side texture
requirements are assigned to different subpasses, and assigns
subpass-specific resources directly inside them.

Pull Request: https://projects.blender.org/blender/blender/pulls/156664
